    "factsheet": [
        {
            "heading": "Aldgate district",
            "paragraphs": [
                "Aldgate straddles two boroughs – City of London and Tower Hamlets, and sits at the intersection of the Square Mile and the East End. From Roman origins, to its medieval history as a gateway into the capital, and throughout the centuries a place where immigrants settled and made a home, the area repays further exploration."
